cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, dataset, or analysis pipeline,
  please cite both the companion paper and the Zenodo deposit
  using the metadata below.
title: >-
  Deep Learning Instance Segmentation for Wound Healing Assays --
  Annotated Image Dataset, Trained Models, and Analysis Pipeline
abstract: >-
  Companion code repository for the manuscript "Deep Learning
  Instance Segmentation for Quantitative Analysis of Cell Migration
  in Wound Healing Assays: A Benchmark and Web-Accessible Tool"
  submitted to Cytometry Part A (2026). Provides the statistical
  analysis pipeline (Pearson, Lin's CCC, Bland-Altman, TOST) and
  paired ImageJ vs AI measurements (n = 225). The associated
  annotated image dataset (n = 1,149) and four trained PyTorch
  model weights are archived at Zenodo under the concept DOI
  10.5281/zenodo.20298129.
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-05-25"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/nykemariotto/scratch-assay-segmentation"
url: "https://huggingface.co/spaces/nmariotto/Scratch-assay-segmentation"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.20298129
    description: >-
      Zenodo concept DOI that always resolves to the latest
      version of the deposit (dataset + models + analysis pipeline).
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.20298130
    description: >-
      Zenodo version DOI for v1.0.0 specifically (the version
      archived for this study).
keywords:
  - instance segmentation
  - wound healing assay
  - scratch assay
  - HUVEC
  - SKOV-3
  - YOLOv11
  - Roboflow 3.0
  - RF-DETR
  - brightfield microscopy
  - Segment Anything Model
  - deep learning
  - cell migration assays
